\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 > What software did you use to create your data visualization?\
	I used python. Specifically the seaborn library.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2     > Who is your intended audience? \
    	Policy makers, but also the public\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2     > What information or message are you trying to convey with your visualization? \
    	With this viz, I focused more specifically on potential COVID transmission in ICUs\'97I wanted to explore the possibility that COVID might be passing around in the ICUs\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2     > What aspects of design did you consider when making your visualization? How did you apply them? With what elements of your plots? \
    	I wanted to use the stack plot to be able to show the proportional distribution of + vs - COVID cases amongst patients in the ICU\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2     > How did you ensure that your data visualizations are reproducible? If the tool you used to make your data visualization is not reproducible, how will this impact your data visualization? \
    	I used a publicly available and provincially maintained dataset. The data comes directly from the provincial government so it is vetted. Given that I am submitting my code alongside this document, my plot should be reproducible \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2     > How did you ensure that your data visualization is accessible?  \
    	I used a colourblind friendly palette\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2     > Who are the individuals and communities who might be impacted by your visualization?  \
    	This viz makes the point that at no point did new COVID cases in the ICU exceeded the number of recoveries. This is an important insight because it shows that ICU units are able to contain disease vectors\'97despite them being overwhelmed with respect to infrastructure (the point I made in Viz 1). However, this point should be taken with caution\'97there might be an unknown threshold after which the infrastructure burden might impair the ability to contain COVID vectors within the ICU. If this were the case, then the stack plot would look different (as if the labels swapped)\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2     > How did you choose which features of your chosen dataset to include or exclude from your visualization? \
    	There were several other geographic regions in this dataset. Additionally, the datapoints ranged from 2020-2024. I focused on my own geographic area and used the most recent year as my datapoints. I wanted to keep my focus consistent across my two visualizations. \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
